 ;; ── the measurement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :measurement
 {:receipt "90-docs/kotobase-performance/2026-08-18-the-cold-isolate-rate-is-not-one.edn"
  :question "when a request DOES hydrate, is L1 warm?"
  :answer {:cold 6 :warm 4 :n 10 :cold-rate 0.6}
  :why-it-was-never-asked
  "Twelve bare /_diag/hydrate reads had reported `sampled: false` twelve times,
   and that was read as `every request lands on a cold isolate`. It is not the
   same claim. A bare diagnostic read does not hydrate; it can only report on
   isolates that happened to have hydrated earlier. The question the cost
   depends on needed a probe that hydrates AND a diagnostic on the same
   connection."
  :confound "ten requests in ~35 s warm the isolates the next may land on, so
             0.6 is an upper bound on coldness under traffic and a lower bound
             for an idle graph. Carried as a parameter, not folded in."}

 ;; ── the defect it exposed, which is the SAME defect as iteration-03 ─────────
 :the-control-caught-it-twice-in-one-session
 {:first "iteration-03: `workerd-scale` was calibrated 2397/1976, the measured
          CPU moved to 2058, and every CPU-neutral hypothesis was priced as a
          +339 ms regression. h5-engine-pin -- the measured zero -- read
          -$6.78. Fixed with `:cpu-ms :unchanged`."
  :second "iteration-04: the class-B baseline moved 84 -> 50.4 while the
           hypotheses still carried the cold-case literal 84. h5 immediately
           read -$12.10. Fixed with `:class-b-ops :unchanged` and by scaling
           every cold-case count by `cold-isolate-rate`."
  :the-shape "A stale literal on EITHER axis reappears as a regression the
              hypothesis does not cause. Both times the ONLY reason it was
              caught is that a hypothesis with a measured zero is sitting in the
              roadmap where its number can be read. A control is not decoration
              in a loop whose inputs are re-measured."
  :both-controls-now {:h5-engine-pin 0.0 :h3-engine-materialisation 0.0}}

